    ],
    "timeout_ms": 5000,
    "set_semantics": false,
    "case_insensitive": false,
    "strict_column_order": false
  },
  "hints": [
    "Next, keep the 2025 lines and decide what one row stands for: one row per store. Then write the total and the tier that labels it.",
    "A CASE can test an aggregate: the WHEN conditions can use the same SUM as the revenue column. Test the 3000000 threshold before the 2000000 one, because the first true branch wins."
  ],
